Abstract:
Conditions for recovering a two-dimensional, time-independent, complex electric potential influenced by gravity from the scattering matrix in a specified energy range are established. Furthermore, an algorithm involving the use of an effective short-range potential is presented to calculate the potential. The effectiveness of this algorithm is demonstrated through an example of an exponential potential. 

